            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of intra-abdominal lipoma--a rare cause of recurrent or acute abdominal pain. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>539-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of an intra-abdominal lipoma is a rare cause of abdominal pain. Two cases are presented--a 21-year-old woman with episodic abdominal pain for 3 years, and a 28-year-old woman with abdominal pain for 4 days before admission to hospital for mechanical small-bowel obstruction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
